h1 -- kbd privacy policy

p -- Effective October 3, 2026

p --
  kbd collects no data. Nothing you type leaves your device. kbd has no network
  access, no accounts, no analytics and no tracking, and it does not use Full
  Access.

p --
  To work, kbd stores a few small files on your iPhone, inside the keyboard's
  own storage: words you add, email addresses you choose to remember, your emoji
  history, and numbers describing where your thumb lands on the keys. They never
  leave your phone, and deleting the app deletes them. kbd also reads your Text
  Replacements and contact names from iOS to offer as suggestions, and keeps
  them only in memory.

p -- Questions: kbd@lavalva.dev
